to get their approval.

229
00:09:25,417 --> 00:09:26,547
But the truth is,

230
00:09:26,837 --> 00:09:29,677
not everyone fixates on what
other people say and do

231
00:09:29,717 --> 00:09:31,097
or obsesses over their rank

232
00:09:31,137 --> 00:09:33,057
in the social hierarchy.

233
00:09:33,887 --> 00:09:35,307
That's just me.

234
00:09:35,387 --> 00:09:37,807
And I've made it
my whole personality.

235
00:09:38,557 --> 00:09:39,607
[AZUMA] Um?

236
00:09:40,437 --> 00:09:42,267
You okay there, Taira?

237
00:09:43,567 --> 00:09:44,687
[AZUMA] Uh?

238
00:09:45,147 --> 00:09:47,397
[TAIRA] People who know
who they are don't change

239
00:09:47,447 --> 00:09:49,067
because of what others do.

240
00:09:49,117 --> 00:09:52,077
They retain their
own independent identity.

241
00:09:52,117 --> 00:09:55,287
I am my own prisoner,
shackled to the social ladder.

242
00:09:55,327 --> 00:09:58,287
Whoa, okay,
I think I'm gonna go.

243
00:09:58,667 --> 00:10:00,957
Whoa! Howdy-do, TairAzuma!

244
00:10:00,997 --> 00:10:02,627
[AZUMA] Please don't ship
real people.

245
00:10:03,167 --> 00:10:05,007
You lovebirds
walking home together?

246
00:10:05,047 --> 00:10:06,087
Yeap!

247
00:10:07,127 --> 00:10:09,087
Hasta mañana!

248
00:10:09,467 --> 00:10:11,847
Okay, see you tomorrow!

249
00:10:12,967 --> 00:10:14,517
[TAIRA]
They're so shameless,

250
00:10:14,597 --> 00:10:16,887
walking side by side like that.

251
00:10:16,927 --> 00:10:19,847
Like they couldn't care less
who sees them.

252
00:10:20,597 --> 00:10:22,307
Kind of inspiring.

253
00:10:22,357 --> 00:10:24,477
Maybe it's time
I had a reinvention arc.

254
00:10:24,477 --> 00:10:26,937
Didn't you just have one,
like, two years ago?

255
00:10:26,987 --> 00:10:28,527
No, shut up.

256
00:10:30,237 --> 00:10:32,237
[Suzuki humming]

257
00:10:35,237 --> 00:10:37,117
- Listen, Suzuki.
- [SUZUKI] Hm?

258
00:10:38,077 --> 00:10:39,077
I've been thinking,

259
00:10:39,117 --> 00:10:40,497
if there's
a certain kind of person

260
00:10:40,497 --> 00:10:41,747
that you're attracted to,

261
00:10:41,827 --> 00:10:44,497
then I should try to become
that kind of person.

262
00:10:44,497 --> 00:10:45,547
That said,

263
00:10:45,797 --> 00:10:47,547
I need you to understand
that I won't be doing

264
00:10:47,627 --> 00:10:49,627
- anything unethical.
- Huh?

265
00:10:50,047 --> 00:10:52,337
Dudes who are rough around
the edges are so hot.

266
00:10:52,387 --> 00:10:55,007
They've got that "I'm damaged,
fix me" rizz, know what I mean?

267
00:10:55,967 --> 00:10:57,057
[Suzuki gasps]

268
00:10:57,217 --> 00:10:59,097
I knew you were
bothered by that!

269
00:10:59,137 --> 00:11:00,387
I'm not bothered by it.

270
00:11:00,517 --> 00:11:02,517
Quit pretending.
If it really didn't bother you,

271
00:11:02,517 --> 00:11:04,227
then you wouldn't have
brought it up!

272
00:11:04,267 --> 00:11:06,227
It's fine. Like I said.

273
00:11:06,277 --> 00:11:07,897
You lie!

274
00:11:07,937 --> 00:11:09,487
[Suzuki laughing]

275
00:11:09,527 --> 00:11:10,647
What now?

276
00:11:11,027 --> 00:11:13,157
Why do you seem happy?

277
00:11:13,197 --> 00:11:15,237
Forget it. [laughs]

278
00:11:16,237 --> 00:11:18,657
- Okay, I'll tell you.
- [sighs]

279
00:11:18,997 --> 00:11:23,287
Tani, I like all kinds of people
for all kinds of reasons.

280
00:11:23,377 --> 00:11:24,667
Especially you.

281
00:11:24,707 --> 00:11:26,127
I get it, it's okay.

282
00:11:26,167 --> 00:11:28,957
I get butterflies in my stomach
if someone looks cool,

283
00:11:29,007 --> 00:11:31,217
or acts cool,
or has a cool personality.

284
00:11:31,257 --> 00:11:32,757
But everyone's
a different kind of cool,

285
00:11:32,797 --> 00:11:34,387
you know what I mean, jellybean?

286
00:11:34,387 --> 00:11:36,387
Yes, I think I do.

287
00:11:36,677 --> 00:11:38,887
That face you're making
is so adorable!

288
00:11:39,887 --> 00:11:41,307
You just keep getting cuter.

289
00:11:41,387 --> 00:11:44,097
- [TANI] Hm?
- It's kinda hard to describe.

290
00:11:44,147 --> 00:11:45,227
But who we like

291
00:11:45,307 --> 00:11:47,857
comes from our own
personal coolness code!

292
00:11:47,897 --> 00:11:49,607
[humming]

293
00:11:51,857 --> 00:11:54,817
You couldn't be
any more adorable!

294
00:11:54,867 --> 00:11:57,617
Daw, Tani!

295
00:11:57,867 --> 00:11:59,157
Uh, Suzuki?

296
00:11:59,197 --> 00:12:01,457
What do you mean by "adorable"?

297
00:12:02,537 --> 00:12:04,747
[distorted]
Cute, tiny Tani.

298
00:12:04,787 --> 00:12:06,747
All for me!

299
00:12:06,787 --> 00:12:09,797
- [Tani groans]
- [TEMPURA] Meow.

300
00:12:10,207 --> 00:12:13,217
- Meow. Meow.
- [TANI] I can't breathe.

301
00:12:14,967 --> 00:12:16,297
- [Tani gasps]
- [meows]

302
00:12:16,347 --> 00:12:17,427
[yawns]

303
00:12:17,467 --> 00:12:19,717
[Tani breathes heavily]

304
00:12:23,437 --> 00:12:25,727
Morning. You got up early.

305
00:12:25,767 --> 00:12:27,767
[TANI] Tempura was on my face.

306
00:12:27,817 --> 00:12:31,357
Oh, my, Tempura,
you adorable little rascal.

307
00:12:33,737 --> 00:12:34,817
[Tempura meows]

308
00:12:37,657 --> 00:12:40,197
Dudes who are rough around
the edges are so hot.

309
00:12:40,237 --> 00:12:42,747
They've got that
"I'm damaged, fix me" rizz.

310
00:12:42,787 --> 00:12:45,787
I like all kinds of people
for all kinds of reasons.

311
00:12:45,827 --> 00:12:46,917
[meows]

312
00:12:46,957 --> 00:12:49,497
[TANI] I told her
it didn't bother me,

313
00:12:49,587 --> 00:12:52,877
but what exactly does
Suzuki find attractive?

314
00:12:55,297 --> 00:12:57,337
Is it strength?

315
00:12:58,297 --> 00:13:01,847
If it is, then I...

316
00:13:03,887 --> 00:13:05,597
[TANI] Mm...

317
00:13:08,857 --> 00:13:10,267
- [TANI] Too heavy.
- [meows]

318
00:13:11,227 --> 00:13:13,527
[SUZUKI] Come on, don't hog it!

319
00:13:13,607 --> 00:13:15,107
Get your giant butt
out of my way.

320
00:13:15,147 --> 00:13:16,657
I've been waiting
a million hours!

321
00:13:16,657 --> 00:13:17,657
Back off, freak!

322
00:13:17,697 --> 00:13:19,407
[both grunting]

323
00:13:19,657 --> 00:13:21,657
[SUZUKI] Mom, where did you
put my gym clothes?

324
00:13:21,657 --> 00:13:23,247
- I'm gonna be late!
- I won't be home tonight,

325
00:13:23,287 --> 00:13:25,497
- I don't need any dinner!
- One at a time, please.

326
00:13:25,537 --> 00:13:26,917
I only have two ears!

327
00:13:28,287 --> 00:13:29,787
Give me a ride halfway!

328
00:13:29,837 --> 00:13:31,497
[SUZUKI'S BROTHER]
What the hell? Get off!

329
00:13:31,957 --> 00:13:33,417
[motorbike approaching]

330
00:13:36,087 --> 00:13:38,547
[SUZUKI] Whoa there, horsie!
Stop right there!

331
00:13:38,637 --> 00:13:41,007
[SUZUKI'S BROTHER]
I am not your horse! Get lost.

332
00:13:41,057 --> 00:13:42,217
[Suzuki laughing]

333
00:13:43,927 --> 00:13:46,637
[sighs] Thanks times a milly!

334
00:13:46,687 --> 00:13:47,637
[TANI] Huh?

335
00:13:47,687 --> 00:13:48,727
♪

336
00:13:50,687 --> 00:13:53,527
Kind of uncharacteristically
gnarly for her.

337
00:13:53,527 --> 00:13:54,687
Don't you think?

338
00:13:54,687 --> 00:13:55,937
I guess.

339
00:13:55,987 --> 00:13:57,357
Where'd she come from?

340
00:13:58,737 --> 00:13:59,987
[Tani sighs]

341
00:14:00,697 --> 00:14:02,117
[Azuma sighs]

342
00:14:02,157 --> 00:14:03,407
Let me guess,

343
00:14:03,697 --> 00:14:06,117
you have no idea who that guy
on the bike with her was.

344
00:14:06,157 --> 00:14:08,037
- I don't.
- Hmm.

345
00:14:08,577 --> 00:14:09,997
Hey, hairball!

346
00:14:10,037 --> 00:14:11,337
Oh, Az...

347
00:14:12,667 --> 00:14:14,207
Tani! [gasps]

348
00:14:14,247 --> 00:14:17,217
Why are you guys here together
at the worst possible time?

349
00:14:17,257 --> 00:14:18,837
[AZUMA]
Good morning to you too.

350
00:14:19,177 --> 00:14:21,467
So, was that your
older brother just now?

351
00:14:21,547 --> 00:14:23,307
- [SUZUKI] Yeah. Gross, right?
- [TANI] Huh?

352
00:14:23,347 --> 00:14:25,597
Motorcycles are so sexy.

353
00:14:25,677 --> 00:14:27,097
Can you introduce me to him?

354
00:14:27,137 --> 00:14:28,307
First of all, no,

355
00:14:28,347 --> 00:14:30,187
second of all,
your taste is awful.

356
00:14:30,227 --> 00:14:31,357
Back me up here, Tani.

357
00:14:31,477 --> 00:14:33,567
Please don't involve me
in this discussion.

358
00:14:33,567 --> 00:14:34,727
[laughs]

359
00:14:36,937 --> 00:14:39,107
- Feel better now?
- [Tani sighs]

360
00:14:40,067 --> 00:14:41,237
Come to think of it,

361
00:14:41,277 --> 00:14:42,867
do you have any siblings, Tani?

362
00:14:42,867 --> 00:14:43,867
[TANI] I don't.

363
00:14:43,867 --> 00:14:46,697
[BOTH] Yeah, checks out.

364
00:14:47,577 --> 00:14:51,037
[TANI] Why did they act
like they expected that?

365
00:14:51,077 --> 00:14:52,207
[AZUMA] So, Suzuki,

366
00:14:52,247 --> 00:14:53,747
does your brother
have a girlfriend?

367
00:14:53,787 --> 00:14:55,497
[SUZUKI] No idea,
but even if he doesn't,

368
00:14:55,587 --> 00:14:57,587
- I'm not gonna give his number.
- [TAIRA] Pigs have flown.

369
00:14:57,587 --> 00:14:58,917
[AZUMA] Aww.

370
00:15:00,757 --> 00:15:01,797
[bell chimes]

371
00:15:02,007 --> 00:15:04,097
[SUZUKI] Time to make
like a tree and leave!

372
00:15:04,137 --> 00:15:05,717
- You go ahead.
- [SUZUKI] Huh?

373
00:15:05,757 --> 00:15:08,267
I'm a library assistant,
so I have to stay and work.

374
00:15:08,307 --> 00:15:10,137
Aw, you never told me that.

375
00:15:10,187 --> 00:15:13,107
No worries,
I'll be fine on my own.

376
00:15:13,187 --> 00:15:15,727
[TANI] Well,
that wasn't convincing.

377
00:15:19,397 --> 00:15:21,357
[Suzuki hums suspiciously]

378
00:15:26,787 --> 00:15:27,827
[GIRL] Hm?

379
00:15:29,457 --> 00:15:30,537
[GIRL] Huh?

380
00:15:32,917 --> 00:15:33,917
[TANI] Hello?

381
00:15:33,957 --> 00:15:35,207
- Suzuki?
- [gasps]

382
00:15:36,167 --> 00:15:37,627
Are you all right?

383
00:15:37,627 --> 00:15:40,837
Oh, yeah, just checkin' out
some, uh, literature.

384
00:15:40,917 --> 00:15:43,967
I realized I've never really
used the library, like, ever.

385
00:15:44,007 --> 00:15:45,097
Isn't that crazy?

386
00:15:45,137 --> 00:15:46,847
I was just waiting
for you to wrap up

387
00:15:46,927 --> 00:15:49,807
and I thought I'd come
look at all these cool books.

388
00:15:49,927 --> 00:15:53,307
Oh, sorry, I'm acting
like such a stalker.

389
00:15:53,347 --> 00:15:54,977
[TANI] I don't think
you are at all.

390
00:15:55,017 --> 00:15:56,937
Really? Oh, thank God.

391
00:15:56,937 --> 00:15:59,067
[TANI] Actually,
if I'm being honest,

392
00:15:59,107 --> 00:16:00,647
I'm happy to see her.

393
00:16:01,067 --> 00:16:04,357
Oh, maybe I should have
told her that just now!

394
00:16:04,407 --> 00:16:08,077
But I don't want her to
wait around for me too long.

395
00:16:08,117 --> 00:16:10,037
Suzuki, you can go if you want.

396
00:16:10,077 --> 00:16:12,287
There isn't much for you
to do here.

397
00:16:12,327 --> 00:16:13,827
[Suzuki gasps]

398
00:16:14,497 --> 00:16:15,577
[TANI] Uh?

399
00:16:15,827 --> 00:16:17,497
Do you think I can't read?

400
00:16:17,537 --> 00:16:19,837
Oh, God, he thinks
I can't read.

401
00:16:19,877 --> 00:16:21,837
No, that isn't
what I meant, I just...

402
00:16:22,837 --> 00:16:24,677
Don't you worry about me!

403
00:16:24,887 --> 00:16:27,887
I'll just grab a book real quick
and head home for today.

404
00:16:30,137 --> 00:16:31,177
[SUZUKI] I get it.

405
00:16:31,427 --> 00:16:33,097
It's annoying having someone
hanging around

406
00:16:33,137 --> 00:16:34,187
when you're working.

407
00:16:34,597 --> 00:16:36,147
Like, when friends show up
to your part-time job

408
00:16:36,187 --> 00:16:38,067
and you can't decide
between being buddy, buddy,

409
00:16:38,107 --> 00:16:39,227
or professional.

410
00:16:43,527 --> 00:16:45,027
[TANI] I messed up.

411
00:16:45,067 --> 00:16:46,987
I thought I was
being considerate,

412
00:16:46,987 --> 00:16:49,027
but she didn't take it
that way.

413
00:16:52,617 --> 00:16:53,577
[TANI] Suzuki.

414
00:16:53,617 --> 00:16:55,497
[SUZUKI] Huh? Oh...

415
00:16:56,167 --> 00:16:59,127
[TANI] The library is going
to close at five o'clock.

416
00:16:59,167 --> 00:17:00,497
Wait for me?

417
00:17:00,877 --> 00:17:02,627
[Suzuki gasps]

418
00:17:03,547 --> 00:17:06,007
Hmm. Mm-hm. Mm-hm.
[chuckles]

419
00:17:08,047 --> 00:17:09,507
♪

420
00:17:21,107 --> 00:17:22,227
[girl gasps]

421
00:17:23,737 --> 00:17:24,777
[girl breathes uneasily]

422
00:17:24,857 --> 00:17:25,897
♪

423
00:17:26,197 --> 00:17:27,777
[TANI] Up until now,

424
00:17:27,857 --> 00:17:28,867
I went through life

425
00:17:29,117 --> 00:17:31,027
taking things people said
to me literally.

426
00:17:31,027 --> 00:17:34,907
Completely missing everything
under the surface.

427
00:17:34,957 --> 00:17:37,167
It didn't matter to me
if my intentions

428
00:17:37,207 --> 00:17:39,627
were conveyed properly
through my words.

429
00:17:40,087 --> 00:17:42,587
I never gave it
a second thought.

430
00:17:44,797 --> 00:17:47,087
Expressing
my thoughts verbally

431
00:17:47,127 --> 00:17:49,757
and understanding others
hoping to do the same

432
00:17:49,757 --> 00:17:52,427
is difficult to figure out.

433
00:17:52,887 --> 00:17:54,057
I can't help but worry

434
00:17:54,097 --> 00:17:56,597
that there's still
a lot I'm missing.

435
00:18:02,067 --> 00:18:03,067
[Suzuki humming]

436
00:18:04,527 --> 00:18:06,697
[SUZUKI] Hey, Gomapon!

437
00:18:06,777 --> 00:18:08,987
Are you headed home
right now, too?

438
00:18:09,067 --> 00:18:10,697
Well, what does it look like?

439
00:18:11,617 --> 00:18:13,287
[SUZUKI] Whoa, nice e-bike,
very compact! [laughs]

440
00:18:13,327 --> 00:18:14,577
Don't laugh at me.

441
00:18:14,617 --> 00:18:17,247
Go home before it gets dark.
Damn kids.

442
00:18:17,287 --> 00:18:19,077
Okay, bye!

443
00:18:20,917 --> 00:18:23,127
- Sorry, were you waiting long?
- [exclaims]

444
00:18:23,167 --> 00:18:24,707
[Suzuki laughs]

445
00:18:24,957 --> 00:18:27,087
I just saw
Gomapon leaving school

446
00:18:27,087 --> 00:18:29,967
on the teeniest little
baby bike! [laughs]

447
00:18:29,967 --> 00:18:32,007
What's so strange about that?

448
00:18:32,097 --> 00:18:33,467
Watching him fried me!

449
00:18:33,507 --> 00:18:36,347
The bike was way too tiny
for his not-tiny body!

450
00:18:36,387 --> 00:18:38,227
The wheels looked like
little biscuits!

451
00:18:38,267 --> 00:18:41,017
The whole thing was
so adorable, I was dying!

452
00:18:41,097 --> 00:18:42,977
[TANI] There it is again.

453
00:18:43,017 --> 00:18:44,107
Quick question.

454
00:18:44,397 --> 00:18:46,737
When you see something
and say that it's "adorable,"

455
00:18:46,817 --> 00:18:47,937
what do you mean?

456
00:18:47,987 --> 00:18:49,657
Huh? You don't know?

457
00:18:49,817 --> 00:18:51,197
Not exactly.

458
00:18:51,407 --> 00:18:54,577
I understand how you might find
a kitten or a panda adorable,

459
00:18:54,617 --> 00:18:56,537
but when it comes
to our faculty members

460
00:18:56,577 --> 00:18:58,707
and their vehicles,
I don't quite follow.

461
00:18:58,747 --> 00:19:00,827
Oh, now I see.

462
00:19:00,827 --> 00:19:03,997
Huh, what's a better way
for me to describe it?

463
00:19:03,997 --> 00:19:06,207
I guess it's sort of like
getting my heart squeezed,

464
00:19:06,247 --> 00:19:08,047
but in a sweet and happy way?

465
00:19:10,127 --> 00:19:11,717
Oh!

466
00:19:11,757 --> 00:19:13,847
It's endearing!

467
00:19:14,467 --> 00:19:16,427
Does that make any more sense?

468
00:19:16,517 --> 00:19:17,597
♪

469
00:19:17,967 --> 00:19:20,347
I guess guys don't toss
around the word "adorable"

470
00:19:20,387 --> 00:19:21,767
all that much, huh?

471
00:19:24,727 --> 00:19:26,317
Later!

472
00:19:26,357 --> 00:19:28,897
I'll have to keep going
to the library from now on!

473
00:19:28,987 --> 00:19:31,027
The book I got
is part of a series!

474
00:19:31,027 --> 00:19:33,447
Oh, I've actually read
that one too.

475
00:19:33,487 --> 00:19:37,157
Really? Once I'm done,
we can talk about it!

476
00:19:38,037 --> 00:19:40,037
Oh, maybe you could recommend

477
00:19:40,037 --> 00:19:41,667
some big brain books
for me to read!

478
00:19:41,707 --> 00:19:43,207
Really? You want me to?

479
00:19:43,247 --> 00:19:44,417
Yeah! I mean,

480
00:19:44,667 --> 00:19:47,337
our tastes are probably
totally different. [giggles]

481
00:19:47,377 --> 00:19:48,627
But that's still fun!

482
00:19:48,667 --> 00:19:50,167
I mean, it's not like
we need to be

483
00:19:50,167 --> 00:19:52,217
carbon copies
of each other, right?

484
00:19:55,797 --> 00:19:57,217
The way I see it,

485
00:19:57,257 --> 00:20:00,057
we'll keep on getting
to know each other, bit by bit.

486
00:20:00,097 --> 00:20:02,557
Then when one of us says,
"Yo, I like this,"

487
00:20:02,597 --> 00:20:05,357
the other can say,
"Yeah, I know you do."

488
00:20:05,397 --> 00:20:08,317
I wanna know all the
little things about you.

489
00:20:13,237 --> 00:20:15,367
- Suzuki, I...
- Hm?

490
00:20:15,407 --> 00:20:16,447
[Suzuki gasps]

491
00:20:18,077 --> 00:20:20,657
[TANI] I don't think
I can ever be like SudaKen

492
00:20:20,697 --> 00:20:23,667
or perfectly fit your
"coolness code,"

493
00:20:23,707 --> 00:20:24,917
but...

494
00:20:26,127 --> 00:20:27,837
[Suzuki exclaims]

495
00:20:29,497 --> 00:20:30,547
[Suzuki gasps]

496
00:20:31,547 --> 00:20:33,047
You're adorable.

497
00:20:34,427 --> 00:20:36,927
[Suzuki exclaims]

498
00:20:37,847 --> 00:20:39,467
Do you understand?

499
00:20:39,927 --> 00:20:42,927
[Suzuki speaking gibberish]

500
00:20:43,477 --> 00:20:45,807
[TANI] Okay,
I'll see you tomorrow.

501
00:20:46,557 --> 00:20:48,687
[SUZUKI] Okie-dokie.

502
00:20:49,107 --> 00:20:50,477
[meows]

503
00:20:54,317 --> 00:20:55,947
[Suzuki exclaiming]

504
00:21:01,947 --> 00:21:03,367
Oh, Tani.

505
00:21:03,617 --> 00:21:05,827
What's up, my guy?

506
00:21:05,867 --> 00:21:07,377
Good morning.

507
00:21:09,997 --> 00:21:12,297
- Listen, Tani.
- [TANI] Mm?

508
00:21:12,337 --> 00:21:14,337
I talked to Suzuki earlier,

509
00:21:14,377 --> 00:21:16,337
and I asked her the reason
she picked you.

510
00:21:16,377 --> 00:21:18,547
Dude, come on,
what is your damage?

511
00:21:18,887 --> 00:21:20,847
She said she likes
how you don't change

512
00:21:20,887 --> 00:21:22,307
who you are for other people.

513
00:21:22,347 --> 00:21:23,347
Oh.

514
00:21:23,387 --> 00:21:25,387
What in the hell
do you mean, "oh?"

515
00:21:25,437 --> 00:21:26,557
It's just...

516
00:21:26,687 --> 00:21:28,437
why would you go out
of your way to tell me?

517
00:21:28,477 --> 00:21:29,517
[TAIRA] Huh?

518
00:21:29,897 --> 00:21:31,777
Because the best compliments
are the ones people give

519
00:21:31,817 --> 00:21:33,777
when you're not around
to hear them. Are you stupid?

520
00:21:34,107 --> 00:21:35,357
♪

521
00:21:35,527 --> 00:21:37,527
You know, I think I'd rather be
around to hear them.

522
00:21:37,567 --> 00:21:39,487
No, no, dude,
people totally glaze you

523
00:21:39,527 --> 00:21:41,157
when they tell you nice things
to your face,

524
00:21:41,157 --> 00:21:42,407
everyone knows that!

525
00:21:42,447 --> 00:21:44,157
They say how they really feel
in the darkness,

526
00:21:44,157 --> 00:21:45,577
where you won't see
the knife coming.

527
00:21:45,617 --> 00:21:47,867
Speaking of darkness,
tone it down, man.

528
00:21:48,207 --> 00:21:49,287
Wait a second.

529
00:21:49,327 --> 00:21:50,997
Were you just trying
to cheer Tani up?

530
00:21:50,997 --> 00:21:53,707
Doesn't that go against
your whole misanthrope thing?

531
00:21:53,757 --> 00:21:54,757
Taira,

532
00:21:55,047 --> 00:21:57,427
- you're a really good person.
- [Taira gasps]

533
00:21:58,757 --> 00:22:00,717
What did you
just call me, you freak?

534
00:22:00,757 --> 00:22:02,637
I am a disgusting
cesspool of negativity,

535
00:22:02,677 --> 00:22:04,387
and while trying to clear
the rot from my soul,

536
00:22:04,427 --> 00:22:05,427
I said something nice,

537
00:22:05,517 --> 00:22:06,597
that does not make me
a good person!

538
00:22:06,637 --> 00:22:09,147
Wow, that was a lot.

539
00:22:09,437 --> 00:22:10,857
Is that a new manga?

540
00:22:10,897 --> 00:22:12,017
[SUZUKI] No, girl, it's a book!

541
00:22:12,147 --> 00:22:14,187
When's the last time
you even read a boo...

542
00:22:14,317 --> 00:22:15,857
- Oh?
- What?

543
00:22:15,897 --> 00:22:17,397
[SATOU] That's a weird combo.

544
00:22:17,447 --> 00:22:18,777
[WATANABE] Super weird.

545
00:22:18,817 --> 00:22:20,617
I cut her off before
she stole two hours...

546
00:22:20,657 --> 00:22:23,367
- [SUZUKI] Huh?
- [SATOU] "Huh" indeed.

547
00:22:23,407 --> 00:22:25,407
Tani's actually
smiling for once.

548
00:22:25,447 --> 00:22:27,077
- That's a new one.
- [Suzuki stuttering]

549
00:22:27,157 --> 00:22:28,247
But why?

550
00:22:29,577 --> 00:22:31,207
This isn't happening.

551
00:22:31,207 --> 00:22:34,417
Does he think those guys
are funnier than me?

552
00:22:34,497 --> 00:22:36,507
That's the part
you're worried about?

553
00:22:36,877 --> 00:22:38,837
[♪ closing theme song playing]
